## Reflection

This project introduced state updates where the circuit modifies its own stored value instead of simply storing external data.

I learned how a counter increments on every rising clock edge when enabled, making it one of the simplest examples of a sequential circuit with internal state progression.

Counters are widely used for timers, frequency division, clocks and control logic in digital systems.

## Problems

No major problems occurred during this project.

The main challenge was understanding that the next value depends on the current stored value rather than only on the external inputs.

